{"type": "answer", "run_id": "retrieval-part2-lean-rest-20261111", "scenario": "eval:retrieval", "source": "real", "setting": "small_lean", "setting_def": {"piece_chars": 600, "k": 4, "rerank": false, "router": false}, "drafter": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "qid": "Q13", "request_id": "retrieval-part2-lean-rest-20261111-small_lean-gpt-oss-120b-Q13", "start_time": "2026-11-11T04:38:49.921+00:00", "degraded": false, "reply": {"request_id": "retrieval-part2-lean-rest-20261111-small_lean-gpt-oss-120b-Q13", "question": "In H-Net, what do the encoder and decoder networks do, and at what resolution do they run?", "kind": "answer", "level": 0, "text": "The encoder network first processes the raw input sequence, compressing it into chunked, richer representations while preserving fine‑grained details for later use [S1][S3].  \nThe decoder network receives the up‑sampled output of the main network and combines those coarse‑grained representations with the fine‑grained details passed through residual connections from the encoder [S3].  \nThe encoder operates on the original, full‑resolution data before down‑sampling, and the decoder operates after up‑sampling back to the original resolution [S1].", "sources": [{"sid": "S1", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.2 §1", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:600:0012", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p02-b008"]}, {"sid": "S2", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.4 §2.1.1", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:600:0026", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p04-b013"]}, {"sid": "S3", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.5 §2.1.2", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:600:0031", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p05-b011"]}, {"sid": "S4", "cite": "2507.07955v2 p.9 §2.4", "pid": "dynamic_chunking:600:0069", "paper": "dynamic_chunking", "block_ids": ["dynamic_chunking-p09-b008"]}], "notice": "checked for citations only (no second-model check)", "eta_s": null, "model_calls": [{"step": "draft", "model": "openai/gpt-oss-120b", "status": 